From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Minimal Linux Live <mll@example.com>
Date: Fri, 06 Mar 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] efi/libstub: add chainloader capability to x86 EFI stub

Extend the Linux kernel EFI stub so that, before committing to the
normal kernel boot, it reads a configuration file from the EFI system
partition:

  \EFI\BOOT\mll_next_boot.cfg

If the file is present and contains a non-empty EFI application path,
that application is loaded via LoadImage() and started via StartImage()
instead of booting the kernel.  This allows a running system to arrange
for an alternate bootloader or OS to be started on the next reboot
without modifying firmware boot-order variables.

Config file format (plain ASCII, one meaningful line):

  \EFI\path\to\app.efi
      Always chainload this target on every boot.

  once:\EFI\path\to\app.efi
      Chainload this target once.  The config file is overwritten with
      a comment before StartImage() is called so that subsequent boots
      return to the normal kernel boot sequence.

  Lines beginning with '#' and blank lines are ignored.

If the config file is absent, empty, a comment, or if LoadImage()
fails for any reason, efi_chainloader_check() returns silently and the
caller continues with the normal kernel boot sequence unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Minimal Linux Live <mll@example.com>
---
